menu "Hisilicon"

config SND_I2S_HI6210_I2S
	tristate "Hisilicon I2S controller"
	select SND_SOC_GENERIC_DMAENGINE_PCM
	help
	  Hisilicon I2S

config SND_SOC_HISTB_AIAO_I2S
	tristate "HiSTB AIAO I2S ports"
	depends on ARCH_HISI || COMPILE_TEST
	help
	  Say Y or M here if you want to use the I2S ports of the AIAO audio block
	  found on HiSilicon STB SoCs such as the Hi3798MV100. Each port is an I2S
	  master with its own clock generator and its own ring-buffer engine, and
	  on these boards the transmit port wired to the HDMI transmitter is what
	  carries its audio. The receive port taps the serial stream of that
	  transmit port back in.

endmenu
